    "avatar": "MG",
    "content": "Can someone explain the derivation of v² = u² + 2as in a simple way?",
    "reactions": [],
    "attachment": null,
    "createdAt": "2026-08-03T14:20:00.000Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "m11",
    "communityId": "class-10-see",
    "channelId": "doubt-solving",
    "author": "Roshan Adhikari",
    "role": "Physics Teacher",
    "avatar": "RA",
    "content": "Start from v = u + at, substitute t into s = ut + ½at², then eliminate t. The two equations combine to give the relation directly.",
    "reactions": [{ "emoji": "🙏", "count": 5 }],
    "attachment": null,
    "createdAt": "2026-08-03T14:25:00.000Z"
